From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] query_cache: EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_FORCE makes every occlusion report
 read as visible, as a test

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series), off unless EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_FORCE=1 is set. A test,
never a fix.

Ocarina's water surface switches on and off whole from one game frame to the next. This asks one
question whatever path the game reads its reports through (a render condition, a macro, the CPU):
is an occlusion report the switch? Each ZPass report gets a rising value, 0x10000 a report, so a
report and the difference of two reports are never 0. The real count is kept for the running
accumulation. SemiFlushQueryDirty skips these reports, or it would write the real count first.

If the water stays on, occlusion reports are the gate. If it still flips, they probably aren't. One
limit: a word the game clears before the report lands still reads 0, so run it with
EDEN_NX2_COND_MODE=always to close the render condition path too.

Cost: nothing is occlusion culled, so expect a lower frame rate, and effects that scale with a
count (lens flare, glows) may show at full strength. Judge the water only. Unset, nothing changes.
Not built, not run.
---
 src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h b/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
--- a/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/query_cache/query_cache.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <array>
+#include <atomic>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <deque>
 #include <memory>
@@ -33,6 +34,16 @@
 namespace VideoCommon {
 
 using Maxwell = Tegra::Engines::Maxwell3D;
+
+/// EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_FORCE=1: every occlusion report reads as visible, a test and never a fix. Each
+/// report gets a rising value, so a report, or the difference of two, is never 0.
+inline bool ForceZpassReports() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_FORCE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
 
 struct SyncValuesStruct {
     VAddr address;
@@ -294,3 +305,8 @@
+        if (ForceZpassReports() &&
+            streamer->GetId() == static_cast<size_t>(QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64)) {
+            static std::atomic<u64> forced{};
+            query_base->value = forced.fetch_add(0x10000, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 0x10000;
+        }
         if (True(query_base->flags & QueryFlagBits::HasTimestamp)) {
             u64 timestamp = impl->gpu.GetTicks();
             std::memcpy(pointer_timestamp, &timestamp, sizeof(timestamp));
@@ -591,6 +607,10 @@
     }
     if (True(query_base->flags & QueryFlagBits::IsFinalValueSynced) &&
         False(query_base->flags & QueryFlagBits::IsGuestSynced)) {
+        if (ForceZpassReports() &&
+            location.stream_id.Value() == static_cast<u32>(QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64)) {
+            return false;
+        }
         auto* ptr = impl->device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(query_base->guest_address);
         if (True(query_base->flags & QueryFlagBits::HasTimestamp)) {
             std::memcpy(ptr, &query_base->value, sizeof(query_base->value));
